    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf a `relative=editor` floating window covers (almost) the entire height of a `:terminal` window and is then closed, the terminal's content is left visually misaligned/misrendered (can be observed with claude code).\n\n<img width=\"609\" height=\"176\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/52cfa1b9-0194-4f32-bd77-fc3afe2e34bb\" />\n\nBy calling a redraw manually, the issue is fixed.\n\nRelated https://github.com/ibhagwan/fzf-lua/issues/2778\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- repro.lua\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"<leader>k\", function()\n    local buf = vim.api.nvim_create_buf(false, true)\n    local win = vim.api.nvim_open_win(buf, false, {\n        relative = \"editor\",\n        width = vim.go.columns, height = vim.go.lines,\n        row = 0, col = 0, border = \"none\",\n    })\n   vim. api.nvim_win_close(win, true)\nend)\n```\n\n- steps\n\n1. `nvim --clean -u repro.lua`\n2. `:terminal`\n3. (this issue is more noticeable with claude code; not sure what if it affects other programs) `claude`\n4. restore a session / create a chat that is \"long enough\" to cover the whole screen\n5. exit to normal mode and trigger the problematic keymap with `<leader>k`\n6. return to insert mode and insert some text: now the prompt text is misaligned\n\nA keymap has to be used, as otherwise neovim may call a redraw.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThere's no misalignment :)\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1006+g31ad7d4527\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.1.4\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.27.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
