            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> By calling a redraw manually, the issue is fixed.\n\nThis is not true, actually. The command `redraw[!]`, by itself, has no effect. The workaround is **exiting command mode, when ui2 is enabled**. I haven't looked at its (ui2's) internals, but I wasn't able to recreate the effect with a simple call to `nvim__redraw()` (admittedly, I haven't tried too hard).\n\nAlso, I noticed that specifying `border` is required for reproducing.",
